# Memory Lapse on a copy of a spell: a copy is not a card (CR 707.10), so when it is countered it ceases to exist rather than
# being put on top of any library (CR 111.7, 704.5d). Bot2 casts an Ornithopter; Bot1 responds with a Lose Focus replicated
# once, its copy aimed at the Ornithopter too; Bot2 answers the copy with Memory Lapse. Bot1's library keeps its size - the
# copy is not in it, and neither is the original, which resolves, finds Bot2 with one mana left of three and no way to pay
# {2}, and counters the Ornithopter into Bot2's graveyard.

